1
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:53,270
...what has turned into a
classic Formula 1 season.

2
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,249
...with the weather
conditions so uncertain,

3
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:00,650
the drivers prepare for...

4
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,929
...the track is still
dangerously wet,

5
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:07,249
but following a drivers meeting,
a decision has been taken.

6
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,920
Three minutes to go.
Everybody off the grid now.

7
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:29,169
25 drivers start every
season in Formula 1,

8
00:01:29,170 --> 00:01:32,260
and each year, two of us die.

9
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:36,419
What kind of person
does a job like this?

10
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:38,959
Not normal men, for sure.

11
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,099
Rebels,

12
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,459
lunatics,

13
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:43,130
dreamers.

14
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:45,999
People who are desperate
to make a Mark

15
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,300
and are prepared to die trying.

16
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:52,039
My name is Niki Lauda,

17
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:55,239
and racing people know
me for two things.

18
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:58,410
The first is my
rivalry with him.

19
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:09,019
What about Hunt? Has he changed?

20
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:10,559
No, he's going on wets.

21
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:13,529
I don't know why it
became such a big thing.

22
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:18,069
We were just drivers busting
each other's balls.

23
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:20,269
To me this is perfectly normal,

24
00:02:20,270 --> 00:02:22,499
but other people saw
it differently,

25
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,000
that whatever it was
between us went deeper.

26
00:02:41,990 --> 00:02:44,089
The other thing I'm
remembered for

27
00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:47,759
is what happened on
1st August 1976,

28
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:50,820
when I was chasing
him like an asshole.

29
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:22,199
Yeah, that's the one. On the
second shelf. Thank you.

30
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,429
Trauma trolley, please.

31
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:26,129
I think the racetrack telephoned
ahead that I was coming.

32
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:27,970
Hunt. James Hunt.

33
00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:36,009
What's the matter? No one ever
seen a spot of blood before?

34
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:38,770
- Are you all right?
- Absolutely fine.

35
00:03:41,550 --> 00:03:43,769
We all thought you'd
been in an accident.

36
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:44,849
I have.

37
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:46,529
If you call a
friendly disagreement

38
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:49,050
with another driver an accident.

39
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,299
What did you disagree about?

40
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,160
It's none of your business.

41
00:03:59,130 --> 00:04:00,160
Sorry.

42
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,030
His wife.

43
00:04:04,170 --> 00:04:06,039
That's going to need a
couple of stitches.

44
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,339
- It's a nasty cut.
- It was a nasty blow.

45
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:10,440
Done with a bloody crowbar.

46
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:14,079
- Why? What did you do?
- Nothing.

47
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,740
Only what she asked me to do.

48
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:20,150
Which was...?

49
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:23,750
I'd be happy to show
you if you like.

50
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,159
Sorry.

51
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:32,969
I have a theory why women
like racing drivers.

52
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:35,739
It's not because they
respect what we do,

53
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:38,239
driving round and
round in circles.

54
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,209
Mostly they think
that's pathetic

55
00:04:40,210 --> 00:04:42,239
and they're probably right.

56
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,730
It's our closeness to death.

57
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:48,779
The closer you are to death,
the more alive you feel.

58
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:52,389
The more alive you are. And
they can see that in you.

59
00:04:52,390 --> 00:04:54,380
They feel that in you.

60
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:57,329
My name is James Hunt.

61
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:59,459
My father is a stockbroker,

62
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,559
my sister is a barrister

63
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,169
and my brother is an accountant.

64
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:05,719
And I,

65
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,250
well, I do this.

66
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:14,009
It's a wonderful way to live.
It's the only way to drive.

67
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:16,810
As if each day is your last.

68
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:28,359
I've never been to a
Grand Prix before.

69
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,019
You still haven't.

70
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:32,930
- This is Formula 3.
- What's that?

71
00:05:33,290 --> 00:05:35,759
That's a lower division,

72
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:38,529
where idiots like me mess about

73
00:05:38,530 --> 00:05:41,899
in the hop of being
talent-spotted to race in F1.

74
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:44,069
- You look disappointed.
- No.

75
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:47,239
You only slept with me because
you thought I was famous.

76
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,940
That's not true!

77
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,749
Don't worry. I will be one day.

78
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:53,149
Morning, everyone.

79
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:55,120
- This is Nursie.
- Gemma.

80
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:58,419
Nursie, this is Bubbles
Horsely, team manager.

81
00:05:58,420 --> 00:05:59,949
How do you do?

82
00:05:59,950 --> 00:06:01,489
- Bubbles?
- Yeah.

83
00:06:01,490 --> 00:06:03,789
Doc Postlethwaite, our designer.

84
00:06:03,790 --> 00:06:05,159
How do you do?

85
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:08,790
And Alexander, Lord
Hesketh, the team's owner.

86
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:11,730
How do you do?

87
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,529
Fine, thanks.

88
00:06:13,530 --> 00:06:15,839
Well done, Superstar!

89
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:18,139
- That's the car?
- Yep, that's her.

90
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:19,540
Lotus 59.

91
00:06:19,910 --> 00:06:22,739
1000cc. Cosworth Mae engine.

92
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:25,940
She's no beauty, but
goes like the slappers.

93
00:06:32,150 --> 00:06:34,389
Nothing to be worried about.
Does it before every race.

94
00:06:34,390 --> 00:06:37,029
Good sign, actually.
Means he's stoked.

95
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:39,729
All Formula 3 cars to
the assembly area.

96
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:41,130
Now, please.

97
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:55,270
...drivers please bring them
to the scrutineering bay now.

98
00:06:55,910 --> 00:06:57,809
All right, Superstar?

99
00:06:57,810 --> 00:06:59,379
Never better, patron.

100
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:01,850
- Have a gargle with this.
- Thank you.

101
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,889
Quick toke of this.

102
00:07:05,890 --> 00:07:09,189
At Crystal Palace today,
James Hunt's on pole,

103
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:12,759
with Austrian newcomer
Niki Lauda alongside him

104
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,499
and Dave Walker
completing Row 1.

105
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:18,429
Row 2 is Mike Beuttler
and Dave Morgan,

106
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:20,199
with Tony Trimmer
and Gerry Birrell.

107
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,339
Who's that?

108
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:22,390
He's new.

109
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,930
- Some German.
- Austrian.

110
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,209
He's been here since 5 a.m.
walking the track.

111
00:07:29,210 --> 00:07:31,949
You might actually have to
concentrate today, James.

112
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,680
You'll need these.

113
00:07:34,050 --> 00:07:36,020
Okay, start her up.

114
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:39,030
Ah! What music!

115
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,059
They could never
have imagined it,

116
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:43,489
those pioneers who
invented the automobile,

117
00:07:43,490 --> 00:07:45,459
that it would possess
us like this,

118
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:48,029
in our imaginations, our dreams.

119
00:07:48,030 --> 00:07:50,529
Nursie, men love women,

120
00:07:50,530 --> 00:07:52,499
but even more than that,

121
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:55,090
men love cars!

122
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:06,210
- Come on, James!
- It's James! Go on, James!

123
00:08:07,150 --> 00:08:08,450
Go, James!

124
00:08:16,090 --> 00:08:17,329
Hunt's still in the lead,

125
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,020
but Niki Lauda is
right on his tail!

126
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:31,339
Hunt and Lauda are proving to
be in a class of their own.

127
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:33,469
They're leaving the
pack far behind.

128
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:36,030
Herr Red Devil's on his tail.

129
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:43,250
Lauda takes a look
down the inside...

130
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:47,010
...and he's sold him a dummy!

131
00:08:49,890 --> 00:08:52,429
Lauda is through!
He's in the lead!

132
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:55,880
Hunt will be determined to
make up for that mistake.

133
00:09:01,770 --> 00:09:03,469
Hunt's in Lauda's slipstream.

134
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:06,070
Lauda's not leaving any gap.

135
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:12,409
The Lotus goes for the inside.

136
00:09:12,410 --> 00:09:14,710
It's an aggressive
move from Hunt.

137
00:09:19,090 --> 00:09:20,680
There's contact!

138
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:31,069
The leaders have spun out!
Lauda's facing the wrong way!

139
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:33,330
The back marker's gone through!

140
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:36,039
You can see why Hunter's
fellow drivers call him.

141
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,770
"Hunt the Shunt."

142
00:09:41,210 --> 00:09:42,209
Asshole!

143
00:09:42,210 --> 00:09:44,149
- Go on, James!
- The Kraut's out of it!

144
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:46,079
Lauda is clearly furious.

145
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:49,279
There's every reason to expect
sharp words in the pit.

146
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:51,519
It's going to be
victory for Hunt.

147
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:55,010
It's going to be an ignominious
defeat for Niki Lauda.

148
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:02,859
So James Hunt scores his
third major Formula 3 win

149
00:10:02,860 --> 00:10:04,999
of the season here,
at Crystal Palace,

150
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,839
after a desperate
battle with Niki Lauda.

151
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,839
Lauda was unable so restart

152
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:12,739
after Hunt's aggressive move
caused them both to spin out

153
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:15,039
in the last lap of the race.

154
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,879
Hard luck. Better
luck next time.

155
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:18,000
Hey, asshole!

156
00:10:19,810 --> 00:10:22,179
That was my line. I
had that corner.

157
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:23,949
You mean the one
that you spun out of

158
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:25,789
and finished facing
the other way?

159
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:27,559
I think that corner had you.

160
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,289
That move was total suicide.
What if I hadn't braked?

161
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:33,029
- We'd have crashed.
- But we didn't, did we?

162
00:10:33,030 --> 00:10:36,260
Thanks to your impeccable
survival instincts.

163
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,530
Fuck you! What's your name?

164
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:43,200
James Simon Wallis Hunt.

165
00:10:43,570 --> 00:10:45,839
Remember it, my
little Jerry friend.

166
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:48,939
- Jawohl! Remember ze name.
- It's very simple.

167
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,279
Hunt, it rhymes with cunt!

168
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:54,540
A word that happens to
describe you perfectly.

169
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:56,149
Who was that?

170
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:59,450
I've no idea. He looks
like a rat, doesn't he?

171
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,519
In my hometown, Vienna,

172
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,829
my family's famous
for one thing:

173
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:05,950
Business.

174
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,959
My grandfather was
a businessman,

175
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,520
my father, too.

176
00:11:11,130 --> 00:11:14,429
So when they heard I wanted
to race cars for a living,

177
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:16,300
They are a few things to say.

178
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,160
Good.

179
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,819
So if my family wasn't
going to help me,

180
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:09,359
I decided to risk everything
and take out a Loan myself.

181
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:12,289
I found a Formula 1
team with an Ok car

182
00:12:12,290 --> 00:12:14,599
and an owner who had
run out of money

183
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,929
and was willing to
accept my terms.

184
00:12:16,930 --> 00:12:18,969
And so, ladies and gentlemen,

185
00:12:18,970 --> 00:12:20,769
I'm delighted to say...

186
00:12:20,770 --> 00:12:23,439
that the winner of the Guild
of Motoring Writers Award.

187
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,739
Driver of the Year...

188
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,140
is James Hunt.

189
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:31,870
Superb news!

190
00:12:32,810 --> 00:12:34,910
- Well done, James.
- Superstar!

191
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,280
Fantastic!

192
00:12:39,150 --> 00:12:40,819
- Well done.
- Thank you so much.

193
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:41,959
Yes!

194
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:45,260
My parents always wanted
me to be a doctor

195
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:48,499
or a stockbroker or something.
They gave me

196
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,769
the first-class education, but
that went all terribly wrong

197
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,200
and I ended up with you lot.

198
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:59,270
Thank you. I need it
more than you do.

199
00:13:00,170 --> 00:13:02,409
I mean, I have a hot head,

200
00:13:02,410 --> 00:13:04,479
an inability to
tolerate discipline...

201
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,179
- Yes!
- Very true!

202
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:08,779
I fall out with people
left and right.

203
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:10,789
The only creatures
I've ever really loved

204
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,280
or treated honorably
are budgerigars.

205
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:18,029
So in any normal area of
life, I'd be, or I am,

206
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:19,529
a total liability.

207
00:13:19,530 --> 00:13:21,999
The only thing I've got going
for me is I'm quick in a car.

208
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,129
So thank you for this and
for acknowledging that.

209
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:25,999
I'm going to give
it to my father

210
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,469
and tell him to put
it on the mantelpiece

211
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:30,400
and imagine it's a first-class
degree in medicine.

212
00:13:44,850 --> 00:13:46,819
Well done, Superstar.

213
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:48,159
Another season like that,

214
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,559
I'll move you up
to the big time.

215
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:51,329
Come on, you don't
think I'm ready now?

216
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,559
You are.

217
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:54,899
I'm not. I've got to
find you a car first.

218
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:56,499
Well, go on, then.

219
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,199
Chop chop. Don't wait too long.

220
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:59,899
You don't want him to
do what Lauda just did.

221
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:02,839
- Why? What did he do?
- Got himself a drive, with BRM.

222
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,939
How the hell did he do that?
He's a nobody.

223
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,309
He's never won a bloody thing.

224
00:14:06,310 --> 00:14:08,409
Apparently, took out a
Loan and bought his way in

225
00:14:08,410 --> 00:14:10,279
with two million
Austrian shillings.

226
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:11,440
Jesus.

227
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:31,899
Niki Lauda.

228
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:34,460
Here for pre-season testing.
BRM?

229
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:38,740
Sign the release form. I'll
let them know you're here.

230
00:14:50,050 --> 00:14:51,819
- Mr. Stanley.
- Good morning.

231
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:53,750
- Good morning.
- Clay!

232
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:57,419
Let me introduce you to
our number one driver.

233
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,190
Clay Regazzoni.

234
00:15:00,790 --> 00:15:02,790
- How are you?
- Good.

235
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,269
Pleasure.

236
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:06,829
And these are your mechanics.

237
00:15:06,830 --> 00:15:09,360
They're reporting
exclusively to you,

238
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:11,309
as per contract.

239
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:12,409
Pleasure.

240
00:15:12,410 --> 00:15:14,840
- Do you wanna see the car')
- Sure.

241
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,540
Hello.

242
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,380
There she is. P160.

243
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:29,680
- Same as Regazzoni's?
- Identical in every detail.

244
00:15:29,990 --> 00:15:31,789
How much does she weigh?

245
00:15:31,790 --> 00:15:34,359
- 600 kilos.
- But that's crazy.

246
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:37,059
- Why so heavy?
- It's a V12 engine.

247
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:40,129
That lump weighs
190K on its own.

248
00:15:40,130 --> 00:15:41,100
Okay.

249
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:44,769
What horsepower are you getting?

250
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:47,369
- No, no, 450.
- It's not enough.

251
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:48,809
It needs to be 500.

252
00:15:48,810 --> 00:15:50,439
And the engine needs to be.

253
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,279
- We already tried.
- Tried what?

254
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,279
Everything

255
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,779
We replaced the entire
exhaust system.

256
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:58,380
- Barely made the difference.
- Are you using magnesium parts?

257
00:16:11,230 --> 00:16:12,529
Now the engine block.

258
00:16:12,530 --> 00:16:15,469
Any mounting or fixing
plates, strip it out also.

259
00:16:15,470 --> 00:16:16,899
When you've done that,

260
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:18,839
we have to look at
the aerodynamics,

261
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,530
front and rear wing.

262
00:16:37,730 --> 00:16:40,090
Okay, thank you. Good night.

263
00:17:00,110 --> 00:17:02,380
What was Regazzoni's time?

264
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,989
1:53.

265
00:17:04,990 --> 00:17:08,289
Okay, now put him in my car and
he'll go 2 seconds faster.

266
00:17:08,290 --> 00:17:11,260
- Well, that's impossible.
- No chance.

267
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:16,399
We've been working
on it all night.

268
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,869
Put Regazzoni in the car.
See what happens.

269
00:17:18,870 --> 00:17:20,329
I don't understand. Why
am I supposed to do this?

270
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:21,339
I don't know, Clay.

271
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:23,830
He wants you to
take it for a spin.

272
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:26,230
Gloves, please.

273
00:18:11,990 --> 00:18:14,819
- I'd say we push it...
- All right.

274
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:17,089
What did you do to the car?

275
00:18:17,090 --> 00:18:18,929
That's information
I'll share with you

276
00:18:18,930 --> 00:18:20,889
under certain conditions only.

277
00:18:20,890 --> 00:18:21,920
Go on.

278
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:25,169
A guaranteed place in the team.

279
00:18:25,170 --> 00:18:26,869
And a paid contract
on equal terms

280
00:18:26,870 --> 00:18:29,169
with Regazzoni for two years.

281
00:18:29,170 --> 00:18:30,699
Are you crazy?

282
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:33,069
Clay's a senior figure in F1.

283
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,739
You're just a rookie!

284
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:37,409
The only reason we took you on
is because you're paying us.

285
00:18:37,410 --> 00:18:39,779
Well, as of now, if
you want me to stay,

286
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:42,279
we rip up the contract,
I don't pay you a cent.

287
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,119
That's outrageous!

288
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,380
Was he quicker in my car?

289
00:18:46,850 --> 00:18:48,820
He was, wasn't he?

290
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:51,910
Did he go two seconds faster?

291
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,690
Two point three.

292
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:01,969
So, have a think,

293
00:19:01,970 --> 00:19:05,100
work out your priorities
and get back to me.

294
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:20,450
Hey, Niki.

295
00:19:23,190 --> 00:19:26,389
I know what you're going to say,
that it's none of my business.

296
00:19:26,390 --> 00:19:27,360
What?

297
00:19:28,730 --> 00:19:32,130
If it's the track manager you're
taking on your date tonight.

298
00:19:33,070 --> 00:19:34,839
It's none of your business.

299
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:37,069
Okay, but if you want my advice,

300
00:19:37,070 --> 00:19:38,870
I'd let this one go.

301
00:19:39,770 --> 00:19:43,000
I'm not questioning your taste.
She is a great girl, but...

302
00:19:45,050 --> 00:19:47,209
Agnes' last boyfriend

303
00:19:47,210 --> 00:19:49,379
was a British Formula 2 driver

304
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:51,789
who has a reputation
for two things,

305
00:19:51,790 --> 00:19:54,349
for being a little
crazy on the track...

306
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:57,089
and for going all
night and all day

307
00:19:57,090 --> 00:19:59,789
and all night again in bed.
He's a good driver,

308
00:19:59,790 --> 00:20:02,159
but an immortal fuck apparently.

309
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,099
I don't know about you,
but that's not an act

310
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:06,120
I'd like to follow.

311
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,900
But if that doesn't
bother you...

312
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:15,000
What's his name, the driver?

313
00:20:15,910 --> 00:20:17,710
Hunt. James Hunt.

314
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:23,779
You see, you share information

315
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,780
and I share information.

316
00:20:26,090 --> 00:20:28,420
That's what teammates are for.

317
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:42,100
- Where the hell are we going?
- I promise it'll be worth it.

318
00:20:42,470 --> 00:20:44,239
Just keep them closed.

319
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,430
Wait for it.

320
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:47,910
Wait for it.

321
00:20:51,850 --> 00:20:52,849
There.

322
00:20:52,850 --> 00:20:54,110
What do you say?

323
00:20:54,410 --> 00:20:56,010
She's Formula 1.

324
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:58,519
Yes, she is, Superstar.

325
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:01,459
Your brother and I got together
with the bean counters.

326
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:03,519
And since the economics
of F1 are not

327
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:06,229
so significantly different
to the economics of F2,

328
00:21:06,230 --> 00:21:09,129
well, we thought if we were
going to be losing money,

329
00:21:09,130 --> 00:21:12,269
we might as well be doing it on
the big roulette table in F1.

330
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:15,530
You fat, little, inbred beauty.
Come here.

331
00:21:19,910 --> 00:21:23,479
Actually, credit where it's
due, we got the idea from Niki.

332
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:25,079
- Who?
- Lauda.

333
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:27,479
Bought his way in
rather than mess about

334
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,879
in the lower divisions.
I thought

335
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:30,179
"Bloody hell, he's right."

336
00:21:30,180 --> 00:21:32,089
No sponsorship, Superstar.

337
00:21:32,090 --> 00:21:33,449
I hope you approve.

338
00:21:33,450 --> 00:21:37,180
No vulgar logos for
cigarettes or condoms.

339
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,989
Just plain white with the flags.

340
00:21:39,990 --> 00:21:42,050
And racing overalls

341
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:44,190
which read

342
00:21:44,770 --> 00:21:47,460
"Sex. Breakfast of champions."

343
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:51,430
So when do we start?

344
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:55,209
- Soon as you're ready.
- Ready?

345
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:57,870
I've been waiting for
this my whole life.

346
00:21:58,780 --> 00:22:01,110
VILLAGE OF WATKINS GLEN

347
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:11,059
When the season started,
people wondered

348
00:22:11,060 --> 00:22:12,929
whether Lord Hesketh
and his team

349
00:22:12,930 --> 00:22:15,329
of upper-class enthusiasts
were bringing glamour

350
00:22:15,330 --> 00:22:18,130
to the racing community
or just comedy.

351
00:22:18,470 --> 00:22:20,869
Certainly it was the first
time anyone had seen

352
00:22:20,870 --> 00:22:24,000
a Butler sewing oysters
and caviar in the pits.

353
00:22:24,270 --> 00:22:27,169
But they have made
quite an impact.

354
00:22:27,170 --> 00:22:30,779
6th in France, 4th in
Britain and 3rd in Holland.

355
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:33,909
All drivers on the track,
caution flags are out.

356
00:22:33,910 --> 00:22:36,449
A severe crash at the Esses.

357
00:22:36,450 --> 00:22:38,889
Red flag. There's a
car off the track.

358
00:22:38,890 --> 00:22:40,889
And reports are reaching
me that there's been

359
00:22:40,890 --> 00:22:43,119
a serious accident
in qualifying.

360
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:45,329
The identity of the driver
we don't currently have,

361
00:22:45,330 --> 00:22:48,199
but as you can tell from
all the activity going on

362
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:51,929
towards the track, it was clearly
a grave incident indeed.

363
00:22:51,930 --> 00:22:54,499
We will, of course, have more
information as we get it,

364
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:57,960
but it is the sight and sound
of F1 nobody likes to see.

365
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:04,970
- Get your hands off me!
- Hey, come on!

366
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:17,859
Drivers of top stature we've
lost just in the past 4 seasons

367
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:20,050
have included Piers Courage,

368
00:23:20,330 --> 00:23:21,420
Jochen Rindt,

369
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:23,490
Jo Siffert,

370
00:23:24,430 --> 00:23:25,899
Roger Williamson

371
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:28,039
and today, at Watkins Glen,

372
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:30,940
Formula 1 has claimed
another driver.

373
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,969
The Tyrrell team have
withdrawn from the race.

374
00:23:33,970 --> 00:23:36,279
Their places on the grid
will be left empty.

375
00:23:36,280 --> 00:23:38,949
- Terrible.
- They should cancel the race.

376
00:23:38,950 --> 00:23:39,930
Why?

377
00:23:40,450 --> 00:23:43,449
He made a mistake, went
into the corner too fast.

378
00:23:43,450 --> 00:23:44,819
It's his fault.

379
00:23:44,820 --> 00:23:47,049
- Is that right?
- It's obvious.

380
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:49,119
Look at the tyre marks.

381
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:52,459
So says the nobody, who had
to pay for his own drive.

382
00:23:52,460 --> 00:23:54,389
How's that working out
for you, by the way?

383
00:23:54,390 --> 00:23:55,490
Fine.

384
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,929
How is it at the back?

385
00:23:57,930 --> 00:24:00,400
Not planning on being
there for long.

386
00:24:01,270 --> 00:24:04,100
Ten minutes to the warm-up lap.
Ten minutes.

387
00:24:07,340 --> 00:24:08,530
Arsehole.

388
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:13,579
Heading into the Grand Hotel
hairpin, second gear.

389
00:24:13,580 --> 00:24:16,579
Turn in hard, looking
for late apex,

390
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:18,240
gentle with the bar.

391
00:24:19,050 --> 00:24:21,389
Heading into Portier,
second gear,

392
00:24:21,390 --> 00:24:22,719
clip the apex,

393
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:24,459
light brake, stay in second,

394
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:26,359
looking for a good exit.

395
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:28,299
Heading through the
tunnel, gradual right,

396
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:31,259
up through third,
fourth, fifth...

397
00:24:31,260 --> 00:24:33,100
ls Alexander around?

398
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,860
Yes, he was.

399
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,409
He went back to the
house to take a call.

400
00:24:38,410 --> 00:24:40,109
He'll be back shortly.

401
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:43,109
He only wanted to show
me his pride and Joy.

402
00:24:43,110 --> 00:24:45,809
Rhymes with 'boy' if you ask me.

403
00:24:45,810 --> 00:24:47,070
And 'toy.'

404
00:24:47,810 --> 00:24:49,519
God, it's so flimsy.

405
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:52,119
For something that
costs so much.

406
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:55,820
There's no comfort, no
protection, nothing.

407
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:58,859
No, it's just a little
coffin, really.

408
00:24:58,860 --> 00:25:01,760
Surrounded by high-octane
fuel in here.

409
00:25:02,060 --> 00:25:04,760
Being driven round 170 mph.

410
00:25:05,070 --> 00:25:08,400
To all intents and purposes,
this thing's a bomb on wheels.

411
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:11,230
You're James, aren't you?

412
00:25:12,570 --> 00:25:13,540
Yes.

413
00:25:14,980 --> 00:25:16,910
You fit the description.

414
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:18,510
Is that right?

415
00:25:19,550 --> 00:25:21,819
Suzy. Friend of Alex's.

416
00:25:21,820 --> 00:25:23,010
Yeah, yeah.

417
00:25:23,450 --> 00:25:25,080
I know exactly.

418
00:25:26,490 --> 00:25:28,359
What was the description?

419
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,019
Mostly positive in
terms of appearance.

420
00:25:30,020 --> 00:25:32,229
Negative only in
terms of character.

421
00:25:32,230 --> 00:25:34,690
I've been told to avoid you.

422
00:25:34,930 --> 00:25:36,090
By whom?

423
00:25:36,730 --> 00:25:37,999
Alexander.

424
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,029
He says you're a bad boy.

425
00:25:40,030 --> 00:25:42,139
Alexander doesn't know
what he's talking about.

426
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:44,199
I was. I'm not anymore.

427
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,269
The new me is very professional.

428
00:25:46,270 --> 00:25:48,009
Early to bed, early to rise.

429
00:25:48,010 --> 00:25:49,340
All very dull,

430
00:25:49,740 --> 00:25:51,179
but according to the team,

431
00:25:51,180 --> 00:25:54,309
the best way to keep beating
the goose stepper.'

432
00:25:54,310 --> 00:25:56,249
Is that what you were
doing when I came in?

433
00:25:56,250 --> 00:25:59,189
Yes, visualization techniques,
memorising the circuit,

434
00:25:59,190 --> 00:26:01,920
in this case Monaco,
which is up next.

435
00:26:06,790 --> 00:26:09,229
Personally I've always
been a great believer

436
00:26:09,230 --> 00:26:11,159
in getting there on the
day, putting my foot down

437
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:13,390
and playing chicken
with everyone else.

438
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:16,469
But they don't want me
doing that anymore.

439
00:26:16,470 --> 00:26:20,100
They want my body like a Temple
and my mind like a monk.

440
00:26:20,940 --> 00:26:23,439
And what about your
soul, your heart?

441
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:25,840
They've got ideas
about that, too.

442
00:26:26,280 --> 00:26:28,419
They want me to stop
messing around,

443
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:31,749
settle down, get married with
the next nice girl I meet.

444
00:26:31,750 --> 00:26:33,949
They think that'd
be good for me.

445
00:26:33,950 --> 00:26:35,459
What do you think?

446
00:26:35,460 --> 00:26:37,480
It sounds fucking awful.

447
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:42,499
But sine they're right
about most things,

448
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:44,960
they're probably right
about that too.

449
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:48,200
You don't fancy getting
married, do you?

450
00:27:13,260 --> 00:27:14,230
Suzy.

451
00:27:15,060 --> 00:27:16,790
JUST MARRIED

452
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:19,260
Hey, hey, hey!

453
00:27:22,700 --> 00:27:25,009
- What's going on with him?
- Nothing. Nothing.

454
00:27:25,010 --> 00:27:27,009
Didn't want to ruin your day.

455
00:27:27,010 --> 00:27:28,130
It's...

456
00:27:28,440 --> 00:27:30,910
- it's the Kraut.
- What about him?

457
00:27:31,980 --> 00:27:34,109
He's just been
signed by Ferrari.

458
00:27:34,110 --> 00:27:35,980
You're kidding me?

459
00:27:36,350 --> 00:27:38,149
Jesus. How did that happen?

460
00:27:38,150 --> 00:27:39,949
Did he buy his way in there too?

461
00:27:39,950 --> 00:27:42,819
Well, the old man
took Regazzoni back

462
00:27:42,820 --> 00:27:45,029
and he insisted
on it apparently.

463
00:27:45,030 --> 00:27:48,220
He says that Niki's a
genius setting up the cars.

464
00:27:55,770 --> 00:27:58,140
FERRARI TEST TRACK
FIORANO, ITALY

465
00:28:06,510 --> 00:28:08,979
It's terrible.
Drives like a pig.

466
00:28:08,980 --> 00:28:11,889
- You can't say that.
- Why not?

467
00:28:11,890 --> 00:28:14,389
- It's a Ferrari!
- It's a shitbox!

468
00:28:14,390 --> 00:28:16,419
It understeers like crazy
and the weight distribution

469
00:28:16,420 --> 00:28:17,889
is a disaster.

470
00:28:17,890 --> 00:28:19,289
It's amazing, all
these facilities

471
00:28:19,290 --> 00:28:21,730
and you make a piece
of crap like this.

472
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:53,929
"Ferrari family,"

473
00:28:53,930 --> 00:28:55,729
"our good friend
Clay Regazzoni."

474
00:28:55,730 --> 00:28:58,059
You are family and friend
to the commendatore

475
00:28:58,060 --> 00:28:59,399
as long as you win.

476
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:00,999
The minute you
don't, ciao, ciao.

477
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:02,499
I totally understand.

478
00:29:02,500 --> 00:29:03,899
It's business.

479
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:05,309
I would do the same.

480
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:07,509
But it isn't just
business, is it?

481
00:29:07,510 --> 00:29:10,139
What we do. It's passion, love.

482
00:29:10,140 --> 00:29:13,109
Which is why we are prepared
to risk our lives for it.

483
00:29:13,110 --> 00:29:14,149
Not me.

484
00:29:14,150 --> 00:29:16,319
If I had more talent and
could earn better money

485
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:18,789
with something else, I would.

486
00:29:18,790 --> 00:29:20,789
How do you know you
will make money here?

487
00:29:20,790 --> 00:29:22,459
You haven't yet.

488
00:29:22,460 --> 00:29:24,650
Not yet, but I will.

489
00:29:25,230 --> 00:29:27,820
If you can, I can.

490
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:34,000
You know, are you
ever not an asshole?

491
00:29:34,330 --> 00:29:36,339
- Why am I an asshole?
- Well...

492
00:29:36,340 --> 00:29:39,909
By now I'm both quicker than you
and better at setting up a car.

493
00:29:39,910 --> 00:29:42,179
You can't deal with it,
so you're the asshole.

494
00:29:42,180 --> 00:29:43,440
Screw you.

495
00:29:50,780 --> 00:29:52,219
I brought you along today

496
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:54,249
because you seem like
a lonely kind of guy.

497
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:56,419
I thought if I introduced
you to some nice people,

498
00:29:56,420 --> 00:29:58,119
that could rub off on you.

499
00:29:58,120 --> 00:29:59,289
Forget it.

500
00:29:59,290 --> 00:30:00,929
Make your own friends.

501
00:30:00,930 --> 00:30:02,359
Come on, Clay.

502
00:30:02,360 --> 00:30:03,760
I'm sorry.

503
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:40,930
Are you leaving?

504
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:42,770
Yes.

505
00:30:43,270 --> 00:30:45,269
Can you give me a lift
to the nearest town,

506
00:30:45,270 --> 00:30:47,800
anywhere with a train station?

507
00:30:48,210 --> 00:30:49,180
Sure.

508
00:30:49,810 --> 00:30:52,109
Trento's half an hour's drive.

509
00:30:52,110 --> 00:30:53,140
Get in.

510
00:31:20,170 --> 00:31:21,839
What are you doing?

511
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:23,909
You hear that noise
when you accelerate?

512
00:31:23,910 --> 00:31:26,179
- No.
- Your fan belt is loose.

513
00:31:26,180 --> 00:31:27,410
My What?

514
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:30,449
And when you brake, your
foot goes all the way down,

515
00:31:30,450 --> 00:31:32,289
which means there's
air in the system.

516
00:31:32,290 --> 00:31:34,450
- Anything else?
- No.

