Come on! What's going on?

1013
01:09:15,480 --> 01:09:19,279
The tyre-changing frenzy caused
a huge reshuffling of the pack,

1014
01:09:19,280 --> 01:09:22,120
- with Mass in the lead now.
- You're clear. Go!

1015
01:09:24,960 --> 01:09:27,150
Lauda urging his
mechanics to hurry.

1016
01:09:29,990 --> 01:09:32,760
It's a disaster! Come on!

1017
01:09:43,710 --> 01:09:45,370
What's going on, you assholes?

1018
01:10:08,830 --> 01:10:11,499
This race has gone
wrong for him so far.

1019
01:10:11,500 --> 01:10:13,439
His championship
rival, James Hunt,

1020
01:10:13,440 --> 01:10:15,460
is a long way up the road.

1021
01:10:25,820 --> 01:10:28,149
Lauda passing car after car.
He's just going past.

1022
01:10:28,150 --> 01:10:30,420
Mario Andretti's Lotus there.

1023
01:11:17,370 --> 01:11:18,340
Niki!

1024
01:11:24,140 --> 01:11:25,470
Get me out!

1025
01:11:25,740 --> 01:11:26,710
Help me!

1026
01:11:29,410 --> 01:11:31,319
Several cars are involved.

1027
01:11:31,320 --> 01:11:33,720
Looks like it might be
one of the Ferraris.

1028
01:11:40,860 --> 01:11:43,190
- Come this way!
- Come on, come on!

1029
01:11:55,470 --> 01:11:56,870
Keep trying

1030
01:12:04,050 --> 01:12:06,180
- Come this way.
- Okay.

1031
01:13:44,150 --> 01:13:47,019
The flood, which swept down Big
Thompson Canyon in Colorado,

1032
01:13:47,020 --> 01:13:49,449
was the worst since
records began.

1033
01:13:49,450 --> 01:13:52,219
In Formula 1 today, victory
celebrations were muted

1034
01:13:52,220 --> 01:13:54,429
after a horrific accident
involving world champion.

1035
01:13:54,430 --> 01:13:56,129
Niki Lauda.

1036
01:13:56,130 --> 01:13:58,159
Due to safety concerns
before the race,

1037
01:13:58,160 --> 01:14:00,459
the Austrian had said
he would not take pan,

1038
01:14:00,460 --> 01:14:02,430
but in the end he did.

1039
01:14:03,230 --> 01:14:05,839
He was making up for lost time
when he went off the track,

1040
01:14:05,840 --> 01:14:08,169
puncturing the
Ferrari's fuel tank.

1041
01:14:08,170 --> 01:14:11,139
Brett Lunger was unable to
avoid the flaming wreck

1042
01:14:11,140 --> 01:14:14,079
but was unhurt and joined other
drivers to rescue Lauda,

1043
01:14:14,080 --> 01:14:17,109
who was taken to Manheim
Hospital with severe burns,

1044
01:14:17,110 --> 01:14:20,749
the incident reminding us again
of the dangers of Formula 1.

1045
01:14:20,750 --> 01:14:22,849
Niki Lauda was trapped
for almost a minute

1046
01:14:22,850 --> 01:14:25,910
in a searing inferno
of 800-plus degrees.

1047
01:16:10,030 --> 01:16:14,960
James Hunt gains on the
absent Niki Lauda.

1048
01:16:18,170 --> 01:16:21,070
28th DAY IN HOSPITAL
29th August 1976.

1049
01:19:12,180 --> 01:19:14,539
- Morning, chaps.
- Hey, here's the man.

1050
01:19:14,540 --> 01:19:15,880
Looking good.

1051
01:19:19,450 --> 01:19:22,019
- What's going on?
- Jesus. It's Niki.

1052
01:19:22,020 --> 01:19:24,219
- What about him?
- He's here.

1053
01:19:24,220 --> 01:19:26,140
- What?
- He's racing.

1054
01:19:41,340 --> 01:19:42,310
Niki.

1055
01:19:49,380 --> 01:19:51,010
It's that bad, huh?

1056
01:19:52,080 --> 01:19:53,050
No.

1057
01:19:54,380 --> 01:19:57,919
In hospital, I asked them
straight, no bullshit,

1058
01:19:57,920 --> 01:20:00,759
how bad my appearance would be.

1059
01:20:00,760 --> 01:20:03,759
They said with time
it would be fine.

1060
01:20:03,760 --> 01:20:05,090
But it won't.

1061
01:20:06,200 --> 01:20:09,220
I can tell, seeing
your reaction.

1062
01:20:10,130 --> 01:20:11,999
I'll spend the rest of my life

1063
01:20:12,000 --> 01:20:14,840
with a face that
frightens people.

1064
01:20:17,170 --> 01:20:20,539
You know, Niki, I tried to write
you a letter at the time,

1065
01:20:20,540 --> 01:20:22,030
to apologise.

1066
01:20:22,780 --> 01:20:25,449
The drivers' meeting in
Germany, before the race.

1067
01:20:25,450 --> 01:20:28,319
- I swayed the room.
- Yes, you did.

1068
01:20:28,320 --> 01:20:31,089
That race should never
have gone ahead.

1069
01:20:31,090 --> 01:20:32,880
No, it shouldn't.

1070
01:20:32,990 --> 01:20:36,889
So in many ways I feel
responsible for what happened...

1071
01:20:36,890 --> 01:20:38,160
You were.

1072
01:20:39,960 --> 01:20:41,190
But, trust me,

1073
01:20:42,800 --> 01:20:45,039
watching you win those races,

1074
01:20:45,040 --> 01:20:47,530
while I was fighting
for my life...

1075
01:20:49,110 --> 01:20:52,770
you were equally responsible for
getting me back in the car.

1076
01:21:20,140 --> 01:21:22,760
- How are you feeling, Niki?
- Fine.

1077
01:21:23,270 --> 01:21:24,269
Niki,

1078
01:21:24,270 --> 01:21:27,839
can you confirm to us exactly
which procedures you had

1079
01:21:27,840 --> 01:21:29,849
and the expectations
for you recovery?

1080
01:21:29,850 --> 01:21:30,840
Sure.

1081
01:21:31,150 --> 01:21:33,149
I had a skin graft operation

1082
01:21:33,150 --> 01:21:36,050
where they put half my
right thigh in my face.

1083
01:21:37,460 --> 01:21:39,650
Now, it doesn't look too good,

1084
01:21:39,960 --> 01:21:42,229
but one unexpected advantage is

1085
01:21:42,230 --> 01:21:44,389
it's impossible to perspire
through a skin graft,

1086
01:21:44,390 --> 01:21:46,799
so sweat will never run
into my eyes again,

1087
01:21:46,800 --> 01:21:49,160
which is good for a driver.

1088
01:21:50,230 --> 01:21:52,269
When they heard about
your condition,

1089
01:21:52,270 --> 01:21:54,909
Ferrari immediately hired
a replacement driver,

1090
01:21:54,910 --> 01:21:56,209
Carlos Reutemann.

1091
01:21:56,210 --> 01:21:59,770
Yeah, before ever
reaching the hospital.

1092
01:22:00,240 --> 01:22:03,510
- Is Reutemann driving today too?
- Yes.

1093
01:22:03,980 --> 01:22:06,049
And keen to make an impression.

1094
01:22:06,050 --> 01:22:08,049
So let's see where
Mr. Reutemann finishes

1095
01:22:08,050 --> 01:22:10,380
and where I finish today.

1096
01:22:11,020 --> 01:22:13,019
James Hunt and McLaren
have caught up a lot

1097
01:22:13,020 --> 01:22:14,989
while you were away.

1098
01:22:14,990 --> 01:22:15,960
Yes.

1099
01:22:16,530 --> 01:22:18,329
So is there a question now

1100
01:22:18,330 --> 01:22:21,260
or are you just trying
to piss me off?

1101
01:22:22,900 --> 01:22:25,299
You still think you can win?

1102
01:22:25,300 --> 01:22:26,999
Yes, of course.

1103
01:22:27,000 --> 01:22:28,490
I have the better car.

1104
01:22:29,040 --> 01:22:31,839
And possibly I'm
the better driver.

1105
01:22:31,840 --> 01:22:34,409
But he's a clever guy and
he's used his time well

1106
01:22:34,410 --> 01:22:37,079
while I was lying
half-dead in hospital

1107
01:22:37,080 --> 01:22:38,910
to win some points.

1108
01:22:40,150 --> 01:22:43,710
And what did your wife say
when she saw your face?

1109
01:22:49,030 --> 01:22:50,820
She said, "Sweetie",

1110
01:22:51,160 --> 01:22:54,220
you don't need a face to drive.
You just need the right foot."

1111
01:22:55,800 --> 01:22:57,200
I'm being serious.

1112
01:22:57,800 --> 01:23:00,539
Do you really think your
marriage can survive

1113
01:23:00,540 --> 01:23:03,030
with the way you look now?

1114
01:23:04,870 --> 01:23:06,930
And I'm being serious too.

1115
01:23:07,580 --> 01:23:08,810
Fuck you.

1116
01:23:09,450 --> 01:23:11,380
Press conference over.

1117
01:23:16,150 --> 01:23:19,419
- That was hairy.
- You know how to get noticed.

1118
01:23:19,420 --> 01:23:21,219
I thought it went
well, to be honest.

1119
01:23:21,220 --> 01:23:23,189
They don't like it when
it's not going their way.

1120
01:23:23,190 --> 01:23:24,829
That's the game.

1121
01:23:24,830 --> 01:23:26,959
- See you.
- See you later.

1122
01:23:26,960 --> 01:23:29,169
- James, are you all right?
- Good, yeah.

1123
01:23:29,170 --> 01:23:31,869
I think I've got something for
you on that last question,

1124
01:23:31,870 --> 01:23:34,610
- About Niki.
- You heard about that?

1125
01:23:36,070 --> 01:23:37,040
James?

1126
01:23:45,480 --> 01:23:47,210
Please, James...

1127
01:23:47,480 --> 01:23:51,150
Now go home to your wife
and ask her how you look.

1128
01:23:53,560 --> 01:23:54,520
Prick.

1129
01:24:11,340 --> 01:24:13,879
So Niki Lauda, just 42 days

1130
01:24:13,880 --> 01:24:16,479
after his near-fatal

1131
01:24:16,480 --> 01:24:18,149
will race here today, at Monza

1132
01:24:18,150 --> 01:24:21,980
against all medical advice and
no doubt in incredible pain.

1133
01:24:26,720 --> 01:24:30,030
Photographers, please,
clear the grid.

1134
01:25:07,430 --> 01:25:09,650
Niki, it's time.

1135
01:25:11,070 --> 01:25:12,320
Okay?

1136
01:25:19,180 --> 01:25:21,110
Please, clear the grid.

1137
01:25:23,280 --> 01:25:25,250
One minute to go.

1138
01:26:11,460 --> 01:26:14,399
The returning Niki Lauda
seems overwhelmed.

1139
01:26:14,400 --> 01:26:17,260
He's been overtaken
by car after car.

1140
01:26:26,410 --> 01:26:29,710
Lauda's off line. He runs
wide onto the grass.

1141
01:26:34,720 --> 01:26:36,789
He wrestles it back
onto the track,

1142
01:26:36,790 --> 01:26:39,080
but that was a bad
moment for Niki.

1143
01:26:43,050 --> 01:26:45,499
Niki Lauda's the
reigning world champion,

1144
01:26:45,500 --> 01:26:48,729
but maybe in his current state
he's a danger out there,

1145
01:26:48,730 --> 01:26:51,790
to himself and to the
rest of the field.

1146
01:26:53,270 --> 01:26:57,369
And Stuck has collided with
Mario Andretti's Lotus!

1147
01:26:57,370 --> 01:27:00,340
Niki's boxed in! He's
got nowhere to go!

1148
01:27:15,090 --> 01:27:17,289
Niki Lauda's actually
making a move.

1149
01:27:17,290 --> 01:27:19,420
He's on Brambilla's tail.

1150
01:27:21,930 --> 01:27:25,069
He pulls out of the
slipstream to overtake.

1151
01:27:25,070 --> 01:27:27,269
Lauda's starting
to find the form

1152
01:27:27,270 --> 01:27:30,100
that early in this race
we believed he'd lost.

1153
01:27:36,150 --> 01:27:38,849
Lauda's now lapping
faster than Reutemann

1154
01:27:38,850 --> 01:27:41,560
and closing the gap ahead.

1155
01:27:44,120 --> 01:27:46,489
Lauda closing on
Carlos Reutemann,

1156
01:27:46,490 --> 01:27:50,420
the man called in to
be his replacement

1157
01:27:58,980 --> 01:28:01,139
And there's James
Hunt's McLaren,

1158
01:28:01,140 --> 01:28:04,440
smoking stationary by
the side of the road.

1159
01:28:06,840 --> 01:28:10,140
This is bad news for
Hunt's championship hopes.

1160
01:28:14,820 --> 01:28:16,289
It's Ronnie Peterson

1161
01:28:16,290 --> 01:28:18,669
who comes home the
winner here at Monza.

1162
01:28:18,670 --> 01:28:21,850
But all eyes are on the man who
finishes a brilliant fourth!

1163
01:28:22,360 --> 01:28:23,830
Niki Lauda!

1164
01:29:05,300 --> 01:29:07,839
What a race, what a
man, what a season.

1165
01:29:07,840 --> 01:29:10,009
With a 4th-place finish and
three priceless points,

1166
01:29:10,010 --> 01:29:12,109
Niki Lauda is a
major step closer

1167
01:29:12,110 --> 01:29:14,910
to retaining the
World Championship.

1168
01:30:12,540 --> 01:30:16,309
So the long, grueling and
incredibly dramatic season

1169
01:30:16,310 --> 01:30:19,239
comes down to this
final race in Japan,

1170
01:30:19,240 --> 01:30:21,770
in the shadow of Mount Fuji.

1171
01:30:22,080 --> 01:30:25,209
Niki Lauda goes into this
deciding race at Fuji

1172
01:30:25,210 --> 01:30:27,519
just three points
ahead of James Hunt,

1173
01:30:27,520 --> 01:30:30,519
Hunt knowing he must beat the
Austrian fair and square

1174
01:30:30,520 --> 01:30:32,570
to take the title.

1175
01:30:33,260 --> 01:30:36,859
James, do you think you can
cope with the pressure?

1176
01:30:36,860 --> 01:30:39,229
Well, I've never really
understood what that means.

1177
01:30:39,230 --> 01:30:42,360
I love my job. I love competing.
I love racing.

1178
01:30:43,330 --> 01:30:45,569
Maybe you should ask Niki.
He's the World Champion.

1179
01:30:45,570 --> 01:30:47,199
He's got everything to lose.

1180
01:30:47,200 --> 01:30:49,509
Mr. Lauda, are you
feeling pressure?

1181
01:30:49,510 --> 01:30:51,810
Do I look like I'm
feeling pressure?

1182
01:30:53,880 --> 01:30:55,279
I'm World Champion

1183
01:30:55,280 --> 01:30:58,349
and on the verge to become
World Champion again.

1184
01:30:58,350 --> 01:31:00,779
Hunt now has the
opportunity to win,

1185
01:31:00,780 --> 01:31:02,549
but it's not so easy
to become a champion.

1186
01:31:02,550 --> 01:31:05,280
You have to really believe
it to make it possible.

1187
01:31:05,590 --> 01:31:08,019
James, is there anything
you'd like to add?

1188
01:31:08,020 --> 01:31:10,419
If Niki is being tricky
and getting a kicky

1189
01:31:10,420 --> 01:31:12,810
out of playing mind games,

1190
01:31:12,860 --> 01:31:14,529
then fine, I'm flattered.

1191
01:31:14,530 --> 01:31:17,930
The fact is momentum is with me.
I've never felt better.

1192
01:31:18,300 --> 01:31:20,769
I fully expect the next press
conference we will have

1193
01:31:20,770 --> 01:31:22,400
will be with me as
World Champion.

1194
01:31:27,010 --> 01:31:29,509
Intermittent heavy
rain has been forecast

1195
01:31:29,510 --> 01:31:32,419
here at Fuji today,
along with strong winds

1196
01:31:32,420 --> 01:31:36,250
rolling in from the mountain.

1197
01:31:38,020 --> 01:31:40,519
And so with today's Japanese
Grand Prix to come,

1198
01:31:40,520 --> 01:31:42,989
Lauda's lead a
mere three points.

1199
01:31:42,990 --> 01:31:44,859
What a way to finish the season.

1200
01:31:44,860 --> 01:31:46,259
Hunt or Lauda?

1201
01:31:46,260 --> 01:31:49,839
The final chapter will unfold when
we bring you extended coverage...

1202
01:31:49,840 --> 01:31:51,199
They've got to cancel the race.

1203
01:31:51,200 --> 01:31:52,569
It's lethal out there.

1204
01:31:52,570 --> 01:31:54,469
The race is going ahead.

1205
01:31:54,470 --> 01:31:56,969
Television rights have been
sold all around the world.

1206
01:31:56,970 --> 01:31:58,339
The showdown between
you and Niki

1207
01:31:58,340 --> 01:31:59,939
is all anyone wants to see.

1208
01:31:59,940 --> 01:32:03,049
With heavy rain continuing
to fall here at Fuji,

1209
01:32:03,050 --> 01:32:05,309
a decision has
finally been made.

1210
01:32:05,310 --> 01:32:09,160
The 1976 Japanese Grand
Prix will go ahead.

1211
01:32:09,890 --> 01:32:12,480
All drivers to
your cars, please.

1212
01:32:36,910 --> 01:32:38,850
Five minutes to go.

1213
01:33:21,220 --> 01:33:22,959
- All right?
- All right.

1214
01:33:22,960 --> 01:33:25,359
- Hold still.
- What the hell are you doing?

1215
01:33:25,360 --> 01:33:27,029
To let the condensation out.

1216
01:33:27,030 --> 01:33:29,899
- It'll also let the water in.
- Not if you're leading.

1217
01:33:29,900 --> 01:33:33,130
Trust me, this race is
all about the start.

1218
01:33:33,770 --> 01:33:36,400
- Need a hand here?
- Yeah, hold it, Teddy.

1219
01:33:51,120 --> 01:33:53,250
Okay, start the bastard.

1220
01:33:55,460 --> 01:33:57,020
Good luck, kid.

1221
01:33:59,300 --> 01:34:00,920
Good luck, James!

1222
01:34:39,240 --> 01:34:41,200
30 seconds to go.

1223
01:35:01,120 --> 01:35:03,329
Electric tension here at Fuji.

1224
01:35:03,330 --> 01:35:05,799
80,000 bedraggled race fans

1225
01:35:05,800 --> 01:35:08,929
and the racing grudge
match of the decade.

1226
01:35:08,930 --> 01:35:11,169
And there's Mario Andretti
in pole position,

1227
01:35:11,170 --> 01:35:13,230
James Hunt alongside him.

1228
01:35:14,400 --> 01:35:16,539
On row two of the grid,

1229
01:35:16,540 --> 01:35:18,109
there is Niki Lauda,

1230
01:35:18,110 --> 01:35:20,939
and on row three of the grid, Joe
Schecketer from South Africa

1231
01:35:20,940 --> 01:35:22,409
in the six-wheel Tyrrell.

1232
01:35:22,410 --> 01:35:25,440
Behind him, the rest
of the 25-car field.

1233
01:35:42,430 --> 01:35:46,800
is underway!

1234
01:35:59,150 --> 01:36:01,749
In this conditions it
must be almost impossible

1235
01:36:01,750 --> 01:36:04,450
to drive a 450-horsepower car!

1236
01:36:31,350 --> 01:36:33,519
And it's Andretti
who has the lead,

1237
01:36:33,520 --> 01:36:34,949
but Hunt is attacking.

1238
01:36:34,950 --> 01:36:37,189
Hunt's going round the
outside of Andretti!

1239
01:36:37,190 --> 01:36:39,049
Niki Lauda following
him through!

1240
01:36:39,050 --> 01:36:42,020
Hunt leads into the
first right-hander!

1241
01:37:24,700 --> 01:37:27,869
Hunt comes through to complete
his first lap leading the field.

1242
01:37:27,870 --> 01:37:30,039
At least he has clear
vision in front of him.

1243
01:37:30,040 --> 01:37:32,970
Niki Lauda behind him,
eating his spray.

1244
01:37:52,090 --> 01:37:53,499
Lauda is slowing!

1245
01:37:53,500 --> 01:37:57,360
Niki Lauda is bringing the Ferrari no.
1 into the pit!

1246
01:37:58,030 --> 01:38:00,839
Some sort of problem,
we can't imagine what,

1247
01:38:00,840 --> 01:38:02,800
so early in the race.

1248
01:38:07,510 --> 01:38:08,940
What's wrong with the car?

1249
01:38:09,550 --> 01:38:11,450
What's wrong with the car?

1250
01:38:12,080 --> 01:38:14,219
Niki! What's wrong with the car?

1251
01:38:14,220 --> 01:38:16,450
Nothing. Car's perfect.

1252
01:38:20,790 --> 01:38:22,319
What are you doing?

1253
01:38:22,320 --> 01:38:23,429
I'm stopping

1254
01:38:23,430 --> 01:38:25,489
His mechanics are asking
what the problem is.

1255
01:38:25,490 --> 01:38:28,059
But wait! Niki Lauda's
getting out of the car!

1256
01:38:28,060 --> 01:38:29,829
This is sensational!

1257
01:38:29,830 --> 01:38:31,999
The reigning World
Champion, Niki Lauda,

1258
01:38:32,000 --> 01:38:33,769
is out of this race.

1259
01:38:33,770 --> 01:38:35,240
It's too dangerous.

1260
01:38:35,440 --> 01:38:37,139
Niki, you want me to say

1261
01:38:37,140 --> 01:38:39,709
there was a problem with
the car, for the media?

1262
01:38:39,710 --> 01:38:40,680
No.

1263
01:38:41,810 --> 01:38:43,240
Tell them the truth.

1264
01:38:43,910 --> 01:38:45,809
Now, what is happening?

1265
01:38:45,810 --> 01:38:47,779
They're talking to
the team manager.

1266
01:38:47,780 --> 01:38:50,220
Lauda explaining something.

1267
01:39:04,900 --> 01:39:08,069
With Lauda out, James Hunt
knows he has to finish

1268
01:39:08,070 --> 01:39:12,109
this race in third place or
higher to be World Champion.

1269
01:39:12,110 --> 01:39:15,079
But the job's not done
yet for James Hunt.

1270
01:39:15,080 --> 01:39:16,879
In these dreadful conditions,

1271
01:39:16,880 --> 01:39:19,400
he still has to go the distance.

1272
01:39:20,720 --> 01:39:22,949
Fifteen laps to go here at Fuji.

1273
01:39:22,950 --> 01:39:24,989
James Hunt or Niki Lauda?

1274
01:39:24,990 --> 01:39:28,059
This extraordinary
season is not over yet.

1275
01:39:28,060 --> 01:39:31,390
In this treacherous final
round, can James Hunt hang on?

1276
01:39:32,130 --> 01:39:35,359
And the scoreboard tells a story.
Lap 58.

1277
01:39:35,360 --> 01:39:37,160
Hunt in the lead.

1278
01:39:38,470 --> 01:39:41,060
Oh, God, his tyres,
they're blistering.

1279
01:39:41,970 --> 01:39:45,909
Brambilla very close behind him,
closing on him all the time.

1280
01:39:45,910 --> 01:39:49,239
And he's trying to drive
inside James Hunt.

1281
01:39:49,240 --> 01:39:52,209
Hunt cuts across the
orange March nose.

1282
01:39:52,210 --> 01:39:54,249
Hunt not having that at all.
And he's spinning.

1283
01:39:54,250 --> 01:39:58,019
He missed Hunt but almost took
James Hunt out of the race

1284
01:39:58,020 --> 01:40:00,059
and out of the world
championship.

1285
01:40:00,060 --> 01:40:03,420
Now we find Mario Andretti
closing on James Hunt.

1286
01:40:07,860 --> 01:40:10,029
Mario Andretti's
going past Hunt!

1287
01:40:10,030 --> 01:40:13,160
Hunt is slowing. James Hunt
seems to have a problem.

1288
01:40:18,410 --> 01:40:20,179
Despite this wet conditions,

1289
01:40:20,180 --> 01:40:22,669
these wet-weather tyres
wear extremely fast.

1290
01:40:22,670 --> 01:40:24,829
Hunt's tyres, they're gone.

1291
01:40:24,830 --> 01:40:28,210
Hunt nursing his car
back to the pit stop.

1292
01:40:30,190 --> 01:40:33,159
That back marker's
going past Hunt.

1293
01:40:33,160 --> 01:40:35,520
LAP 70 4 LAPS TO GO

1294
01:40:44,330 --> 01:40:47,799
Look at that left front tyre,
right front tyre, sorry.

1295
01:40:47,800 --> 01:40:51,069
No tread on it at all. And
the other one is flat.

1296
01:40:51,070 --> 01:40:52,540
Let's go! Let's go!

1297
01:40:57,480 --> 01:41:00,149
Okay? When did you
break your gear lever?

1298
01:41:00,150 --> 01:41:01,949
Nine or ten laps ago.

1299
01:41:01,950 --> 01:41:04,319
- Alistair, we need to lift it!
- Come on!

1300
01:41:04,320 --> 01:41:06,059
- At the front!
- Let's go!

1301
01:41:06,060 --> 01:41:09,159
Regazzoni's Ferrari and
Jacques Lafitte in the Ligier

1302
01:41:09,160 --> 01:41:10,889
have gone ahead.

1303
01:41:10,890 --> 01:41:12,290
Come on, hurry!

1304
01:41:12,830 --> 01:41:15,960
You did it. You're going
to be World Champion!

1305
01:41:16,470 --> 01:41:17,489
Not yet.

1306
01:41:17,490 --> 01:41:21,069
A few laps ago, James Hunt was
looking like champion elect.

1307
01:41:21,070 --> 01:41:23,970
Now it looks as though it's
all gone wrong for him.

1308
01:41:25,370 --> 01:41:26,809
- James.
- Come on!

1309
01:41:26,810 --> 01:41:27,939
- Listen.
- What?

1310
01:41:27,940 --> 01:41:30,309
Just go easy out there.

1311
01:41:30,310 --> 01:41:34,219
- What are you saying?
- I'm saying look after yourself.

1312
01:41:34,220 --> 01:41:36,449
We want you back in one piece.

1313
01:41:36,450 --> 01:41:39,819
You're too far back. There's too
many drivers in front of you.

1314
01:41:39,820 --> 01:41:43,220
- There's always next year.
- So that's it? It's over?

1315
01:41:44,230 --> 01:41:45,190
Clear!

1316
01:41:45,790 --> 01:41:46,760
James!

1317
01:41:48,400 --> 01:41:50,390
- Clear!
- Fuck it!

1318
01:41:54,770 --> 01:41:57,569
James Hunt rejoins the
race in sixth position.

1319
01:41:57,570 --> 01:42:01,810
There are four laps to go.
Surely no way back for the Brit.

1320
01:42:21,400 --> 01:42:23,099
Concentrate, Superstar.

1321
01:42:23,100 --> 01:42:25,099
Just brings it back
under control!

1322
01:42:25,100 --> 01:42:28,070
Sliding the McLaren on
the very edge there.

1323
01:42:29,970 --> 01:42:32,839
Hunt's M23 twitching this
way and that under braking.

1324
01:42:32,840 --> 01:42:34,209
And he almost loses
it right there.

1325
01:42:34,210 --> 01:42:35,809
Hunt on the tail
of Jacques Lafitte

1326
01:42:35,810 --> 01:42:37,370
in the blue Ligier.

1327
01:42:44,990 --> 01:42:46,750
Don't do it, James.

1328
01:42:49,260 --> 01:42:51,029
He's inches away
from the pit wall!

1329
01:42:51,030 --> 01:42:53,150
He's inches away
from the Ligier!

1330
01:43:02,100 --> 01:43:04,309
James Hunt has made
up another place,

1331
01:43:04,310 --> 01:43:07,470
but it's not enough and
this race is running out.

1332
01:43:15,920 --> 01:43:18,850
And Watson has spun!
Watson has spun!

1333
01:43:22,190 --> 01:43:25,229
Hunt manages to weave his
way between the back marker

1334
01:43:25,230 --> 01:43:27,499
and the stationary Penske.

1335
01:43:27,500 --> 01:43:30,129
He's catching Regazzoni,
but in these conditions,

1336
01:43:30,130 --> 01:43:33,760
it's one thing to catch up,
quite another to overtake.

1337
01:43:36,910 --> 01:43:39,469
He's alongside Clay Regazzoni!
This could be

1338
01:43:39,470 --> 01:43:41,410
the world championship!

1339
01:43:49,080 --> 01:43:50,810
He's got him!

1340
01:44:06,240 --> 01:44:08,099
Hunt crosses the line.

1341
01:44:08,100 --> 01:44:11,209
He needed to finish third
to score enough points

1342
01:44:11,210 --> 01:44:12,809
to be World Champion,

1343
01:44:12,810 --> 01:44:15,139
and in the confusion
here we're being told

1344
01:44:15,140 --> 01:44:16,879
that he may have finished 5th.

1345
01:44:16,880 --> 01:44:18,010
He finished fifth?

1346
01:44:19,250 --> 01:44:21,849
Our lap charts show
Hunt in third place.

1347
01:44:21,850 --> 01:44:23,719
Well, if the scoreboard's right,

1348
01:44:23,720 --> 01:44:26,359
it means he's just missed
out on the championship.

1349
01:44:26,360 --> 01:44:29,980
Crushing defeat for Hunt
after such a heroic drive.

1350
01:44:33,960 --> 01:44:36,229
I can see the race
stewards conferring,

1351
01:44:36,230 --> 01:44:38,499
examining the
official lap charts.

1352
01:44:38,500 --> 01:44:41,730
We're just going to have to
wait for their verdict here.

1353
01:44:58,390 --> 01:44:59,859
Let's get you out
of here, buddy.

1354
01:44:59,860 --> 01:45:02,119
I'm sorry, Teddy. I thought
I could make up the ground.

1355
01:45:02,120 --> 01:45:04,229
Sony? What are you talking about?
You did it!

1356
01:45:04,230 --> 01:45:07,129
- Did what?
- Jesus! You crazy bastard!

1357
01:45:07,130 --> 01:45:09,769
You came 3rd! You
got the points!

1358
01:45:09,770 --> 01:45:11,399
You're champion of the world!

1359
01:45:11,400 --> 01:45:14,439
James Hunt is now
officially confirmed

1360
01:45:14,440 --> 01:45:17,039
as finishing third
here in Japan,

1361
01:45:17,040 --> 01:45:20,300
and that means he is
champion of the world.

1362
01:45:22,010 --> 01:45:24,709
Our new World
Champion, James Hunt,

1363
01:45:24,710 --> 01:45:27,240
by just one single point.

1364
01:45:33,060 --> 01:45:34,960
Did we really win?

1365
01:45:38,030 --> 01:45:40,190
World bloody Champion!

1366
01:45:48,970 --> 01:45:52,840
- What are you going to do now?
- I shall be getting drunk.

1367
01:45:53,810 --> 01:45:56,280
It's wonderful, absolute dream.

1368
01:46:42,790 --> 01:46:46,429
And our special guest, Formula
1 champion, James Hunt.

1369
01:46:46,430 --> 01:46:49,090
JAMES HUNT WORLD CHAMPION

1370
01:46:59,010 --> 01:47:01,030
JAMES HUNT AGAINST ALL ODDS

1371
01:47:10,890 --> 01:47:12,910
Wait. Come on.

1372
01:47:15,460 --> 01:47:18,820
There's no better motor
oil than Havoline.

1373
01:47:29,700 --> 01:47:33,009
- Yes, me too. Where we going?
- Anywhere I want to go.

1374
01:47:33,010 --> 01:47:35,479
And I don't have to
hijack it, either.

1375
01:47:35,480 --> 01:47:37,749
As long as I pay for it.

1376
01:47:37,750 --> 01:47:40,180
I'm starving. Let's
get some food.

1377
01:47:46,250 --> 01:47:48,250
BOLOGNA, ITALY

1378
01:47:50,860 --> 01:47:52,829
- Where are you going?
- You lot go ahead.

1379
01:47:52,830 --> 01:47:54,730
I won't be a minute.

1380
01:47:56,260 --> 01:47:57,230
Niki!

1381
01:48:00,240 --> 01:48:01,730
Good to see you!

1382
01:48:06,040 --> 01:48:08,009
I heard you were spending
more and more time

1383
01:48:08,010 --> 01:48:10,249
- in one of these.
- Do you fly?

1384
01:48:10,250 --> 01:48:11,249
No.

1385
01:48:11,250 --> 01:48:13,979
- I don't think they'd insure me.
- You should try.

1386
01:48:13,980 --> 01:48:15,219
It's good for discipline.

1387
01:48:15,220 --> 01:48:16,789
You have to stay
within the rules,

1388
01:48:16,790 --> 01:48:18,489
stick to regulation,
suppress the ego.

1389
01:48:18,490 --> 01:48:20,419
It helps with the racing.

1390
01:48:20,420 --> 01:48:23,159
And there I was thinking you
were about to wax lyrical

1391
01:48:23,160 --> 01:48:26,720
- about the romance of flight.
- No, that's all bullshit.

1392
01:48:28,200 --> 01:48:30,069
So what brings you here?

1393
01:48:30,070 --> 01:48:31,829
A friend's wedding.

1394
01:48:31,830 --> 01:48:33,169
At least I think
it was a wedding.

1395
01:48:33,170 --> 01:48:34,399
Might have been a
birthday or something.

1396
01:48:34,400 --> 01:48:36,069
It's all a bit of a blur.

1397
01:48:36,070 --> 01:48:38,969
- Have you been at Fiorano?
- Pre-season testing.

1398
01:48:38,970 --> 01:48:40,939
- You're relentless.
- Thank you.

1399
01:48:40,940 --> 01:48:42,879
I'm not sure that was
meant as a compliment.

1400
01:48:42,880 --> 01:48:45,749
When do you start testing?
Next week?

1401
01:48:45,750 --> 01:48:47,449
No. What, are you nuts?

1402
01:48:47,450 --> 01:48:49,079
I didn't just win the
biggest thing of my life

1403
01:48:49,080 --> 01:48:51,390
so I could get right
back to work.

1404
01:48:51,790 --> 01:48:54,030
Why? You have to.

1405
01:48:54,490 --> 01:48:56,419
To prove to all the people

1406
01:48:56,420 --> 01:48:58,259
who will always say you
just won it because...

1407
01:48:58,260 --> 01:49:01,700
Because of what? Because
of your accident?

1408
01:49:02,830 --> 01:49:05,769
Niki, is that other
people or is that you?

1409
01:49:05,770 --> 01:49:07,169
I won, okay?

1410
01:49:07,170 --> 01:49:08,969
On the all-important day
when it came down to it,

1411
01:49:08,970 --> 01:49:11,909
we raced on equal terms,
equally good cars.

1412
01:49:11,910 --> 01:49:14,139
And I put my life on the
line and I saw it through.

1413
01:49:14,140 --> 01:49:16,179
- And you call that winning?
- Yes.

1414
01:49:16,180 --> 01:49:18,809
The risks were totally
unacceptable.

1415
01:49:18,810 --> 01:49:20,479
You were prepared to die.

1416
01:49:20,480 --> 01:49:23,019
- To me, that's losing.
- Yes, I was. I admit it.

1417
01:49:23,020 --> 01:49:25,849
I was prepared to die
to beat you that day.

1418
01:49:25,850 --> 01:49:27,859
And that's the effect
you have on me.

1419
01:49:27,860 --> 01:49:30,920
You'd pushed me that far.
And it felt great!

1420
01:49:31,430 --> 01:49:34,059
I mean, hell, isn't that
what we're in this for?

1421
01:49:34,060 --> 01:49:36,860
To stare death in the
face and to cheat it?

1422
01:49:37,770 --> 01:49:39,869
Come on, there's
nobility in that.

1423
01:49:39,870 --> 01:49:41,770
It's like being knights.

1424
01:49:42,070 --> 01:49:44,469
You English, you're
such assholes.

1425
01:49:44,470 --> 01:49:46,739
You know my position.

1426
01:49:46,740 --> 01:49:47,979
20% risk.

1427
01:49:47,980 --> 01:49:50,749
No, Niki, don't bring the
percentages into this.

1428
01:49:50,750 --> 01:49:52,209
Don't be a pro.

1429
01:49:52,210 --> 01:49:54,949
The minute you do that, you
kill what's good about this.

1430
01:49:54,950 --> 01:49:56,710
You kill the sport.

1431
01:49:59,750 --> 01:50:00,720
James!

1432
01:50:01,720 --> 01:50:02,710
James!

1433
01:50:06,390 --> 01:50:07,920
I've got to go.

1434
01:50:09,400 --> 01:50:11,460
Careful in this thing.

1435
01:50:12,430 --> 01:50:13,490
James.

1436
01:50:19,110 --> 01:50:22,700
In hospital, the toughest part
of my treatment was the vacuum.

1437
01:50:23,180 --> 01:50:25,249
Pumping the shit
out of my lungs.

1438
01:50:25,250 --> 01:50:26,770
It was hell.

1439
01:50:27,220 --> 01:50:29,819
And while doing it, I was
watching television.

1440
01:50:29,820 --> 01:50:32,749
- You winning all my points.
- Your points?

1441
01:50:32,750 --> 01:50:35,759
"That bastard, Hunt," I'd say.
"I hate that guy."

1442
01:50:35,760 --> 01:50:37,529
And one day, the
doctor came and said,

1443
01:50:37,530 --> 01:50:40,159
"Mr. Lauda, may I offer
a piece of advice?"

1444
01:50:40,160 --> 01:50:42,399
"Stop thinking of it as a
curse to have been given

1445
01:50:42,400 --> 01:50:43,999
an enemy in life."

1446
01:50:44,000 --> 01:50:45,999
"It can be blessing too."

1447
01:50:46,000 --> 01:50:47,569
"A wise man gets more
from his enemies

1448
01:50:47,570 --> 01:50:49,469
than a fool from his friends."

1449
01:50:49,470 --> 01:50:52,240
And you know what? He was right.

1450
01:50:54,140 --> 01:50:55,479
Look at us.

1451
01:50:55,480 --> 01:50:58,179
We were both a pair
of kids when we met.

1452
01:50:58,180 --> 01:51:00,449
Hot-headed jerks in Formula 3.

1453
01:51:00,450 --> 01:51:03,540
Disowned by our families.
Headed nowhere.

1454
01:51:04,220 --> 01:51:07,089
And now we're both
champions of the world.

1455
01:51:07,090 --> 01:51:08,780
It was not bad.

1456
01:51:09,160 --> 01:51:11,189
No, it's not bad.

1457
01:51:11,190 --> 01:51:13,359
So don't let me down now.

1458
01:51:13,360 --> 01:51:15,259
I need you busting my balls.

1459
01:51:15,260 --> 01:51:18,260
- Get back to work.
- I will, Niki, I will.

1460
01:51:18,800 --> 01:51:21,169
But I intend to
enjoy myself first.

1461
01:51:21,170 --> 01:51:23,739
Some of life needs
to be for pleasure.

1462
01:51:23,740 --> 01:51:26,939
What's the point of having a
million cups, medals and planes

1463
01:51:26,940 --> 01:51:29,410
if you don't have any fun?

1464
01:51:29,880 --> 01:51:32,140
How is that winning?

1465
01:51:33,080 --> 01:51:35,949
- James!
- We're gonna leave without you!

1466
01:51:35,950 --> 01:51:36,940
James!

1467
01:51:41,090 --> 01:51:43,250
I'll see you on race day, champ.

1468
01:51:44,290 --> 01:51:45,450
You will...

1469
01:51:45,890 --> 01:51:46,860
champ.

1470
01:51:49,060 --> 01:51:51,269
You look good, Niki.

1471
01:51:51,270 --> 01:51:55,130
The only guy to have burnt his
face and it be an improvement.

1472
01:52:01,040 --> 01:52:03,740
Of course he didn't
listen to me.

1473
01:52:04,010 --> 01:52:07,249
For James, one world
title was enough.

1474
01:52:07,250 --> 01:52:10,240
He had proved what
he needed to prove,

1475
01:52:10,520 --> 01:52:14,080
to himself and anyone
who doubted him.

1476
01:52:14,990 --> 01:52:17,859
And two years later he retired.

1477
01:52:17,860 --> 01:52:21,060
When I saw him next in
London seven years later,

1478
01:52:21,400 --> 01:52:23,499
me as champion again,

1479
01:52:23,500 --> 01:52:25,229
him as broadcaster,

1480
01:52:25,230 --> 01:52:29,140
he was barefoot on a
bicycle, with a flat tyre.

1481
01:52:29,740 --> 01:52:32,870
Still living each
day like his last.

1482
01:52:34,040 --> 01:52:37,880
When I heard he'd died aged
45, of a heart attack,

1483
01:52:38,180 --> 01:52:40,150
I wasn't surprised.

1484
01:52:40,750 --> 01:52:42,770
I was just sad.

1485
01:52:43,280 --> 01:52:46,250
People always think
of us as rivals,

1486
01:52:46,790 --> 01:52:49,990
but he was among the
very few I liked

1487
01:52:50,830 --> 01:52:53,730
and even fewer that I respected.

1488
01:52:56,900 --> 01:52:59,990
He remains the only
person I envied.

1489
01:53:13,250 --> 01:53:16,800
Born3o.

